    "description": "## Outcome and context\n\nEmily asked whether a Player who is also a BA should link to their BA profile from the Player record — a cross-reference in the same spirit as Related Referrer Record, but pointing to the BA object instead.\n\n## Current state\n\nBUILD-210 (BA-9, WAGR-166) built the reverse direction — a Players Related List on the BA record showing players assigned to that BA. No lookup or link exists on the Player record pointing back to a BA profile when the Player is also a BA.\n\n## Proposed solution\n\n1. Confirm whether this cross-reference is needed given how often (if ever) a Player is also a BA in practice.\n2. If needed, add a lookup or link on the Player record to the corresponding BA record, cross-reference only — same pattern as Related Referrer Record, no merge logic.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. A Player record that corresponds to a BA shows a link to that BA's profile.\n2. A Player record with no matching BA shows no broken or empty link.\n3. No merge logic is introduced between the Player and BA records.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nRelated to BUILD-210 — Brand Ambassador: Players Related List (WAGR-166) and BUILD-174 — Player: Attribution fields (WAGR-43, Related Referrer Record pattern).\n\n## Source\n\nWagertech Notes / Questions (Emily Vandenberg), Player record doc, reviewed Sep 2026: \"If the Player is a BA should it also link to their BA Profile in the Player Object?\" https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mp3b1qpJkzKNDztEQpdnv-BYCgUgDdXe5jLuJi-ix1U/edit?tab=t.0",
